WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.290
Speaker 1: former President Mike Pence has
been doing the rounds mostly to sell his book

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:10.840
and maybe to kind of softly prod at the possibility
of a 2024 presidential run.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.129
And he appeared on a Fox News program called
Outnumbered.

00:00:14.129 --> 00:00:22.400
The gag with Outnumbered is that it's four
female hosts and they invite on a man each

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.130
show and the man is outnumbered.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:27.300
Okay, that's the idea.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.300
Check out.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.350
So context.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.020
This interview that Pence gave is almost as
bad as some of.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.820
Trump's worst interviews.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.250
It's really something to see.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:44.160
Check out how dynamic and funny and clever
and charismatic Mike Pence is right off the

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.160
bat.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.160
And of course, I'm kidding.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.160
He's none of those things.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.220
Speaker 3: Hello, everyone.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.420
This is outnumbered.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:50.859
I'm Emily Companion.

00:00:50.859 --> 00:00:55.860
And joining me today, Carley Shimkus, Martha
MACCALLUM and ainsley earhardt.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:00.930
And we are honored to have on the former vice
president of the United States, Mike Pence.

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.690
It is his first time on Outnumbered.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.500
And sir, we are thrilled and honored to have
you here with us today.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.940
Speaker 2: Oh, it's great to be here.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.250
Although I do feel outnumbered.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:16.530
Speaker 1: You know, it's it's great to be
here.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.030
Carley Shimkus.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:22.010
But I do feel.

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:23.010
Outnumbered.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:27.260
Just charisma dripping off of this guy, reeking
of charisma.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.329
And of course, we're all cringing very, very
hard.

00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:33.119
Now, there were some interesting questions
posed to Pence.

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:36.280
More interesting was, was the way that he
answered these questions.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.350
He was asked, do you want to be the president
of the United States?

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:40.940
Speaker 3: I don't have a lot of time.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:45.590
So I think one of the first ones I want to
ask you is what is on everyone's mind, because

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:49.820
this is a foundation for people understanding
you and your life.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:55.299
We often see books come out from people who
are saying, I want to be president of the

00:01:55.299 --> 00:01:56.460
United States.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:00.650
So my first question is, do you want to be
president of the United States?

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:04.969
Speaker 2: Well, Martha, I would say no more,
no less than any other kid that grew up with

00:02:04.969 --> 00:02:06.329
a cornfield in his backyard.

00:02:06.329 --> 00:02:08.860
Speaker 1: So is that a yes or a no?

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:12.790
Speaker 2: You know, I can tell you the dream
of public service animated my youth as I write

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:19.300
about in the book the opportunity I had to
represent my hometown in Congress to be governor

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:23.660
of Indiana and ultimately to serve as your
vice president is deeply humbling to me.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.080
But Karen and I are going to take time over
the holidays.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.700
You know, we have to in the military so we
would between deployments are our kids have

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:34.830
not all been back in Indiana for the last
three years together.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:39.831
So we'll take time to reflect, deliberate,
talk to the kids and oh, we're going to we're

00:02:39.831 --> 00:02:44.260
going to make a decision about what our next
calling is, but I promise to keep you posted.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.470
Speaker 3: But when you do that, when you.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:53.310
Speaker 1: Yeah, let me interpret this answer
for you in, you know, standard Republican

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:56.640
speak and to some degree politicians speak.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:00.950
I don't know if I'd have a shot at winning
right now, Martha.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:06.940
So what I'm going to do is I'm going to bring
in consultants and pollsters to figure out,

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.270
do I have a shot?

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:14.540
And if I do have a shot, I'm going to probably
try to go for it, particularly if I believe

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:20.180
that even in losing it might raise my profile
or somehow be advantageous to me in some way,

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.180
shape or form.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:27.300
Now, one of the things that is a little bit
different is that as a former V.P., it's one

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:33.280
thing to lose the general election for president
as a former VP.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.580
Happened to Al Gore, for example.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:43.370
But to lose the Republican primary as a former
VP and in particular to run against the president

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:45.390
you served under.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:46.420
That's a little bit different.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.760
And that I don't I don't know.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:49.760
Has that happened in history?

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.120
I don't know off the top of my head.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.700
But that's sort of a different thing and a
different, different consideration.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:58.890
A couple other clips here citing absolutely
no evidence whatsoever.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:06.860
He starts talking about how Twitter and Elon
Musk are being targeted by Biden because of

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:10.160
something related to the Hunter Biden story.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:11.160
Check this out.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.469
Speaker 2: The suggestion that the president
of the United States is keeping a close eye

00:04:15.469 --> 00:04:21.020
on on any element of the media is deeply offensive
to me.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:24.620
It's it's it's your job in the media to keep
a close eye on elected officials.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:29.240
So I lived in that world for 20 years as a
congressman, as a governor, and as your vice

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:30.240
president.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.240
And.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:38.540
But I do think, as you suggest, I think it
may well be because Elon Musk, who I came

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:41.770
to know very well during the four years of
the Trump administration.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:48.310
Well, I think it's because he is preparing
to release information finally about the suppression

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:49.960
of the Hunter Biden story.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:53.570
Speaker 1: So this is like two layers of stuff.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:57.800
First of all, there's no evidence that anything
that's going on has to do with the Hunter

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:58.800
Biden story.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.080
But again, if all you have is a hammer, everything
looks like a nail.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:02.370
Must be related to Hunter Biden.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.370
That's number one.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:08.360
But the funniest and honestly, the scariest
part of this is Pence saying, you know, a

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:11.440
White House keeping an eye on the media.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.840
Trump had a hit list of media people that
he didn't like.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.490
Trump wanted to kick people out of the pressroom.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:21.801
Trump did kick some people out of the press
room like Jim Acosta from CNN briefly, although

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:28.120
he eventually went back, he says it's chilling
or whatever phraseology he used for an administration

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.030
to be keeping an eye on the media.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:38.569
The Trump administration was maybe the modern
administration most adversarial and hostile

00:05:38.569 --> 00:05:42.350
to journalism and to the media and to a free
press.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:43.690
It's absolutely bonkers.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:46.319
Now, one last clip here.

00:05:46.319 --> 00:05:47.950
I won't even introduce this one.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:48.950
Just listen.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:52.430
Speaker 3: I want to ask you a question about
your faith, because we share the same faith.

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:56.400
But how do you know that that is God calling
you?

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.840
Because everywhere you go, people love you.

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:04.199
How even Democrats love you because you're
just a nice, wholesome, good person who does

00:06:04.199 --> 00:06:05.830
the right thing.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:07.229
And and you're honest.

00:06:07.229 --> 00:06:08.229
You're honest.

00:06:08.229 --> 00:06:11.590
But they might not like your politics, but
they like who you are and your character.

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.919
Speaker 1: So I love that.

00:06:13.919 --> 00:06:15.530
First of all, everybody loves you.

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:16.530
Democrats love you.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:18.220
It wasn't Democrats don't love them.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.710
And the MAGA people wanted them killed on
January 6th.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:24.910
So I don't know what on earth Ainsley EARHARDT
is talking about, but I love the question.

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:27.500
How do you know that that's God really speaking
to you?

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.760
It's sort of like one of these things where
Bush said he spoke to God and God told him

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:31.979
to invade Iraq.

00:06:31.979 --> 00:06:37.060
And then, you know, all these stories that
are told, I checked with God and God said

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:39.750
to go ahead to do it or God chose this.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:43.590
Was it maybe just indigestion and God not
really speaking to you?

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.330
I just absolutely love that.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:48.280
How do you know it really is God speaking
to you?

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:54.310
And of course, the question has its own internal
logic for those who believe God speaks to

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:58.000
them or might or speaks to some people.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.310
How do you know that that's really God?

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.810
Speaking to you is a very logical question.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:07.430
They never have an actual good answer, but
it's just so funny to hear Ainsley Earhart

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:08.650
say, How do you know?

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:10.610
And also just everyone loves you.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.400
No, no, that's not true.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:16.240
The Democrats don't love him and half of the
Republicans don't love him.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.220
And some of that half wanted him killed on
January 6th.

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:20.650
Unbelievable stuff.

